  "id": "COMPOUND:27192 - PROTEIN:6147",
  "verbalization": "Fumotonaringin is implicated in the regulation of Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9 through a multi-step mechanism involving thioredoxin, a target of oleamide and cid 20842. The evidence suggests that Fumotonaringin acts as a modulator of the thioredoxin pathway, which in turn influences the activity of the SDR family member 9. This relationship is supported by the presence of multiple indirect pathways, all of which converge on the SDR family member 9 as a downstream target. The scores from the paths indicate a consistent level of confidence in this mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The involvement of thioredoxin, a well-characterized redox regulator, suggests that Fumotonaringin may exert its effects through redox-mediated processes, potentially altering the activity of the SDR family member 9. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the biological network, but the core mechanism remains plausible and biologically relevant.",
